false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.03901634856627334,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":55.6,"_gate_rev_durability":0.17607909997985338,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.10619146540332661,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.024651889794798376,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":80.8,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.007426363590747153,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":87.6,"_gate_insider_own":0.0292,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":19.5,"_gate_insider_buying":0.083,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":8.3,"pf":[],"description_full":"Arch Capital Group Ltd., together with its subsidiaries, provides insurance, reinsurance, and mortgage insurance products in the United States, Canada, Bermuda, the United Kingdom, Europe, and Australia. The company operates through three segments: Insurance, Reinsurance, and Mortgage. The Insurance segment offers commercial automobile; commercial multiperil; financial and professional line liability; admitted, excess, and surplus casualty lines; property and short-tail specialty; workers compensation; and casualty insurance. Its Reinsurance segment provides reinsurance products for casualty; marine and aviation; property catastrophe; property excluding property catastrophe; and other specialty products. The Mortgage segment offers U.S. primary mortgage insurance business written predominantly on loans sold to the Federal National Mortgage Association and Federal Home Loan Mortgage Corporation; reinsurance and underwriting services related to the U.S. credit-risk transfer business and other U.S. mortgage reinsurance transactions; and international mortgage insurance and reinsurance business covering loans. It markets its products through a group of licensed independent retail and wholesale brokers. The company was formerly known as Risk Capital Holdings, Inc. Arch Capital Group Ltd. was founded in 1995 and is headquartered in Pembroke, Bermuda.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Nicolas Alain Emmanuel Papadopoulo | CEO & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $7.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 8K people. Revenue per employee of $2.5M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 13%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $766K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $18K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Arch Capital Group Ltd. is a large-cap financial services business with a $35.7B market cap on $19.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +28% over the past three years and +18% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 21% against a 7% cost of capital \u2014 a 14-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $6.1B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 31 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.40\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 36\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 10.6% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 2.9% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (92% sell ratio, net $8.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 62% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 35% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Research Analysts Offer Predictions for ACGL FY2026 Earnings","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/research-analysts-offer-predictions-for-acgl-fy2026-earnings.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794490175.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.848,"tier":0,"scop